          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பாதசாரி — pātacāri — \"a pedestrian\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பாதசாரிகள் நடைபாதையில் நடக்க வேண்டும். pātacārikaḷ naṭaipātaiyil naṭakka vēṇṭum. Pedestrians should walk on the footpath."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The plural is பாதசாரிகள்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பாதசாரி (pātacāri) is borrowed from Sanskrit pādacārin, \"going on foot, a pedestrian\" (Monier-Williams), from pāda, \"foot\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
